Anyway, I took some advice and dropped requirement from
"expert" to "skilled". I decided against "david's sling" artifact
cause well, I couldn't find a biblical reference to the name of
David's sling. I doubt he named it at all.

But, I left it at 100% kill at skilled because now...

All humanoid giant class monsters die in 1 hit :-p
Titans, Cyclops, Stone Giants... Lord Surtur. Sorry Rogues,
your sling doesn't get to skilled. But wizmode tests show
that indeed, Lord Surtur dies as soon as you hit him with
sling + gem.

The only classes this effects then are: ACHRaW, the only
classes that can get "skilled" in sling.

As for the other feature of this patch, the sling now is the
only launcher that gets dmg bonus from strength. (Daggers
and darts don't got launchers, so obviously, they get
dmg bonus. UNFAIR!!!! )

I doubt either of these additions will make the sling
overpowered. Indeed, rocks are heavy, darts/daggers do
more damage and don't need launcher, darts can be
poisoned, arrows are infinite with LoD on Ranger and
can be poisoned and enchanted to +7 or higher.

The only real gameplay effect is the Caveman. Even
then, I doubt it is an automatic switch.

Caveman endgame:
With new sling patch:
Rocks thrown at +6 (25)str +2 expert +d2 base == 9.5 avg
x2 rocks thrown (d3) == 19 dmg.

Flintstones are too rare for anyone to really use them
as weapons IMO.

arrows +7 enchant +1skilled +d6 poison +d6 base == 15 avg
x1.5 arrows shot ==22.5 dmg

Obviously, it is the arrow's poison that makes the cut. But
sling will be a much better early weapon (max damage only
requires gauntlet of power). Both can be blessed
and deal a bit more damage to undead, but there are
silver arrows avaliable... So bow probably makes a better
choice in the long run.

Wizards don't got skill slots for skilled sling, expert +7 daggers get
strength bonus anyway and are basically infinite ammo. Expert
+7 daggers obviously pwn sling to the ground.

Rangers... Think caveman with bow, except Ranger can shoot
2 more arrows, gets +1 damage cause of expert skill... and infinite
ammo due to LoD. Not to mention, 500 arrows is same weight as
50 rocks. :-/ Wow. I think I'll go with the sling </sarcasm>

Archeologists can sling... but I bet #twoweapon is better. +7 dagger
(no
extra throwing bonus) is still awesome, 2 stones thrown may even
be weaker than 1 dagger thrown. 1.5 * (6 + 1 + d2) == 12.75 average.
7 + 6 + d4 == 15.5 average.

With that said, I think it is easy said that slings *need* this
much of a damage boost, and much much more.
But here is the patch for a start :-p

